Reference colour statistics for the per-board matrix tests. Each file is
JSON written by lib_mgras_matrix.write_stats() and is named
<board>-<feature>.json. Take them from a run that was judged correct by
eye: every run saves a candidate as mgras-<board>-<feature>.stats.json in
its log directory, beside the frame it describes.

One per feature on each board, each from a frame checked by eye:
  si-lit3d.json     ivview draws the lit windmill
  si-pixels.json    imgview shows brick.rgb
  si-t-lit3d.json   as si-lit3d
  si-t-pixels.json  as si-pixels
  si-t-texture.json perfly draws the CH-53 with its panel texture, the
                    rotor blades and the Performer logo
  ssi-lit3d.json    as si-lit3d
  ssi-pixels.json   as si-pixels
  ssi-doublebuffer.json  clock draws its face
  esi-lit3d.json  esi-pixels.json   as the SI two
  esi-t-lit3d.json  esi-t-pixels.json  esi-t-texture.json
                    as the SI+T three
  essi-lit3d.json  essi-pixels.json  essi-doublebuffer.json
                    as the SSI three

A missing file fails the test, as a mismatch does. When a model change
alters a frame on purpose, check the new frame by eye before replacing
its file.
